 "description": "Film looks loaded from the SD card onto the stock art filters (experiments/2026-11-18-stock-filters/design.md), with the menu row Load Looks (data/specs/looks-menu-4.json: Off / Load). Load reads C:\\\\EPM2LOOK.BIN, checks it as card-looks-4 does, keeps it in the EEROM bank's unused tail (store 0x603F8000) and applies it: each listed entry's tables go into its RAM block (data/specs/stock-films-structure.json), then each entry's switch list is written, its film words when the file lists it and its stock words otherwise; the Picture Mode settings 111, 509, 510 follow the stored values of the entries with a hidden value. Every start applies the stored file. The hook on the GUI state setter's trace call 0x7ECDF6E4, the task USRTEST_A. Every expect is a stock byte. Version 6 (experiments/2026-11-20-film-name-exif/NOTES.md): the switch lists of data/specs/stock-films-structure-2.json; at each GUI state T_GUI calls FILMNAME, which writes the EXIF template's ImageDescription (0x605BAEC0): the film's name when the stored Picture Mode is an entry with a film, else Olympus's text. Version 7 (experiments/2026-11-20-model-calibration/NOTES.md \u00a76): the switch lists of data/specs/stock-films-structure-3.json, where an in-place entry with a film also gets no 12-region table. Version 8 (experiments/2026-11-21-firmware-dive/plan.md): the last entry of segment 3's constructor table (0x7F033B78) points at C_START, which applies the stored file in task Usr1 after the segment copies and then runs the entry's constructor 0x7EEC05FF; the task at the first GUI state writes the texts and names, and applies the stored file only if C_START found none. The text table also holds the English texts of the rows Peaking (ids 1505, 1506, 1500) and Lowest S/S Setting (1503, 1504), so both rows show them in every menu language. FLAGS and T_END are no longer at fixed addresses: `_symbols` gives the labels that data/specs/log-menu-3.json hooks. Version 9 (experiments/2026-11-24-af-spot-metering/NOTES.md, build spot-af): the text table also points the ids 1494 and 1509 (unused built-in EVF texts) at the label and help of the row Spot Metering (data/specs/spot-menu.json) in the loaded language.",
